      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This self-directed learning module highlights advances in evaluation and treatment of congenital and acquired musculoskeletal disorders in the child. It is a section of the chapter on pediatric rehabilitation for the Self-Directed Medical Knowledge Program Study Guide for practitioners and trainees in physical medicine and rehabilitation. This section contains information on alterations of limb structure and gait, scoliosis, torticollis, sports injuries and overuse syndromes, and unexplained pain in children."},
